      "card_ids": ["C07"],
      "claim": "The closest analogue, sharing the same N-methylpyrazole and tertiary amide side chain, showed only 15% SUV brain uptake in rats and was labeled poor penetration; however, the report attributes this to reduced lipophilicity, and the query is more lipophilic (logP 3.21), limiting direct transfer.",
      "evidence_role": "contradictory"
    },
    {
      "card_ids": ["C04"],
      "claim": "A close analogue with the same spiro-amine/ether scaffold and an aryl fluoride showed rapid high brain uptake in monkey PET after IV administration, demonstrating that this chemotype can achieve meaningful CNS access despite a basic amine and tertiary amide.",
      "evidence_role": "supportive"
    },
    {
      "card_ids": ["C03"],
      "claim": "Another analogue of the same scaffold with a secondary amide also showed rapid high brain uptake in monkey PET, independently supporting CNS permeability for this scaffold.",
      "evidence_role": "supportive"
    },
    {
      "card_ids": ["C09"],
      "claim": "A further analogue of the same spiro-amine/ether scaffold showed excellent brain penetration in vivo in rat and monkey, reinforcing that this scaffold is CNS-permeable.",
      "evidence_role": "supportive"
    },
    {
      "card_ids": ["C06"],
      "claim": "Vornorexant, an azole-containing amide CNS drug, achieved an unbound CSF/plasma AUC ratio of 0.46 in rats, showing that azole/amide compounds can have meaningful brain exposure.",
      "evidence_role": "supportive"
    }
  ],
  "confidence": "moderate",
  "decision_summary": "Predicted pass: the query is more lipophilic than the poor-penetration closest analogue C07, and the same spiro-amine/ether/amide scaffold is validated by multiple PET analogues (C04, C03, C09) with rapid brain uptake; azole-containing amides such as C06 also show meaningful CNS exposure. The physicochemical prior's low passive-diffusion concern is outweighed by direct experimental evidence from close analogues.",
  "evidence_gaps": [
    "No direct brain/plasma, CSF, or PET measurement for the exact query molecule.",
    "C07's poor SUV may be due to lower lipophilicity; quantitative logD comparison with query is not available.",
    "Efflux transporter status (P-gp/BCRP) for the query is not experimentally characterized."
  ],
